{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "oOZbE",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Auth",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "uPP4L",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Auth — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BKJIf",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 1.0.0 · updated: 2026-09-16\n\n1. PURPOSE\nThe doors into a single-user instance: login, the second factor (ADR-018), password recovery, and the two TOTP screens enrolment reaches. No signup — the one account is created by the first-boot setup wizard (onboarding.pen).\n\n2. ENTRY POINTS\n- Login — / redirects to /login (sessions#new)\n- 2FA and Código de recuperación — only with a pending login, after the password step (/two-factor, /recovery-code)\n- Forgot → Email sent → Reset → Enlace expirado or Contraseña actualizada — \"¿Olvidaste tu contraseña?\" on Login (/forgot-password, /reset-password/:token)\n- TOTP · Alta and Códigos de recuperación — from Ajustes' Seguridad row (/two-factor/setup, /two-factor/codes). Opened from the wizard's Seguridad step (D52) the same screens wear the wizard's frame, drawn in onboarding.pen (D122)\n\n3. SCREENS (left → right)\n- Login · Default · Login · Error\n- 2FA · Código de recuperación\n- Forgot · Email sent · Reset · Enlace expirado · Contraseña actualizada\n- TOTP · Alta · Códigos de recuperación — these two render in the app shell, not the auth card; this file draws the Ajustes entry\n- Desktop band: Login\n\n4. BUSINESS RULES\n- Every screen from Login to Contraseña actualizada renders in layouts/auth: one card, the wordmark inside it on a phone; on desktop the card splits, a brand panel with the wordmark and \"100% libre y open source\" beside the form. Login's desktop artboard stands for all of them (D4)\n- TOTP · Alta and Códigos render in layouts/app with HeaderBar back to Ajustes once the account is onboarded; the nav lights Ajustes. Mid-wizard they render in layouts/onboarding instead, under the step header, and lead on to the summary (D122)\n- Email OTP and SMS are out: a lost authenticator is answered by one-time recovery codes, ten of them, shown once (ADR-018)\n- Email sent says the same thing whether or not the address exists, so the page cannot confirm an account (password_resets/sent.html.erb)\n- The reset window is stated from User::PASSWORD_RESET_EXPIRES_IN, never in prose\n- The codes are not downloadable: the list is select-all and the page warns they are not shown again\n\n5. COPY SOURCE\nconfig/locales/es-MX.yml — auth.*, two_factor.*, totp_enrollments.*. Failure messages: Identity::UseCases::Login, VerifyTotpCode, ConsumeRecoveryCode.\n\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\n- 2FA and Código de recuperación with a wrong code — the Login · Error alert above the form, reading \"Ese código no es válido.\"; TOTP · Alta reads \"Ese código no es válido. Revisa tu app de autenticación.\"\n- Login after the pending second factor timed out — the alert reads \"Se agotó el tiempo para verificar. Inicia sesión otra vez.\"\n- Reset with an invalid password — a negative box listing the model's errors above the fields\n- Login's notices after logout or an expired session — a flash, not the inline alert\n- Desktop for every auth-layout screen — the same split panel Login draws\n- TOTP · Alta when already enrolled — it redirects to Ajustes, or to the wizard's summary mid-wizard\n- Códigos reloaded after they left the session — it redirects with \"Los códigos solo se muestran una vez. Podrás generar unos nuevos desde Ajustes.\"\n- The QR is drawn as an icon; the code renders a real one on a white plate\n\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nNone.\n\n8. HISTORY\n→ Log frame, below this brief.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
